From 82e484d7eaa37ad8dc8cf2f6c975810fad338200 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:17:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] selftests/bpf: exercise ordered CPUMAP migration and
 failures

Exercise source reservations, ring completion, CPU migration, mixed
native/generic traffic, queue-full drops, remote actions, concurrent
producers, entry replacement and CPU hotplug. Ordinary CPUMAP controls
must demonstrate the reordering that the ordered mode prevents.

Add native multi-buffer payload/length checks, including a remote XDP
program. Inject allocation failures only in the selected CPUMAP worker,
require an observed allocation drop, then verify draining and migration
recover. Restore the affected CPU and failslab settings on error paths.

The tests keep a packet blocked on one CPU to distinguish completion
from dequeue. They do not infer packet delivery from a redirect return.

Assisted-by: LLM
